WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.700
Fisherman rib is a comfortable, stretchy,

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.260
wide, fabric that's created
by tucking stitches

3
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.340
when you're doing double bed knitting.

4
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.620
It's reversible, making it a great
choice for scarves and shawls.

5
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.540
The needle setup is 1x1 ribbing.

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.900
Get started by casting on 1x1

7
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.620
with a Cast on that's
really stretchy and loose.

8
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.180
Set your ribber to tuck in one direction

9
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.740
and the main bed to tuck
in the opposite direction.

10
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:36.780
This way, with each pass of the carriage,

11
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.620
one bed will knit while
the other bed will tuck.

12
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:45.020
Be sure and bind off loosely.

13
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:51.460
You'll be pleasantly surprised at the
texture and the width of this fabric.

14
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.940
Would you like to learn
more about your ribber?

15
00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:01.180
Please look for the Knit It Now home study
course called Ribber Basics Boot Camp.

16
00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:07.180
Learn to make more beautiful fabrics like
this Fisherman Rib plus lots, lots more.

17
00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.920
Master your ribbing with Knit it Now.

